@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Log Analytics and Alerts in Azure Monitor";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="lead text-center">Learn how to use Log Analytics and Alerts in Azure Monitor to enhance system observability and proactive monitoring.</p>
    <hr />

    <!-- Introduction -->
    <div class="mt-4">
        <h2 class="text-success">What is Log Analytics?</h2>
        <p>
            Log Analytics is a powerful tool within Azure Monitor that allows you to collect, analyze, and visualize log data from various sources.
            It enables real-time monitoring, troubleshooting, and insights to optimize system performance and security.
        </p>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/log-analytics-overview.jpg" alt="Log Analytics Overview" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Azure Log Analytics provides deep insights into your infrastructure and applications.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Benefits of Log Analytics -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-warning">Benefits of Using Log Analytics</h2>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Centralized Log Management:</strong> Aggregate logs from multiple sources into a single workspace.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Advanced Querying:</strong> Use Kusto Query Language (KQL) to analyze data efficiently.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Real-Time Insights:</strong> Detect performance issues and security threats instantly.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Custom Dashboards:</strong> Create visual dashboards to monitor critical metrics.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Integration with Azure Services:</strong> Seamlessly integrates with Azure Security Center, Sentinel, and more.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Setting Up Log Analytics -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-danger">How to Set Up Log Analytics</h2>
        <ol class="list-group list-group-numbered">
            <li class="list-group-item">Create a Log Analytics workspace in the Azure Portal.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Connect data sources like Virtual Machines, Azure AD, and Application Insights.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Use KQL queries to analyze and filter log data.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Set up dashboards and reports to visualize insights.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <!-- Azure Monitor Alerts -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-primary">Understanding Azure Monitor Alerts</h2>
        <p>
            Azure Monitor Alerts notify you when critical conditions occur in your environment. These alerts help teams respond quickly to potential issues.
        </p>
        <h3 class="text-info">Types of Alerts</h3>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Metric Alerts:</strong> Triggered based on predefined performance thresholds.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Log Alerts:</strong> Triggered by KQL queries evaluating log data.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Activity Log Alerts:</strong> Detect changes in Azure resources.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Application Insights Alerts:</strong> Monitor application performance and failures.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Configuring Alerts in Azure Monitor -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-success">How to Configure Alerts</h2>
        <ol class="list-group list-group-numbered">
            <li class="list-group-item">Navigate to Azure Monitor and select "Alerts."</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Click "Create Alert Rule" and choose the target resource.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Define the condition (e.g., CPU usage exceeds 80%).</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Set up an action group (email, SMS, webhook, etc.).</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Review and create the alert rule.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <!-- Best Practices -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-warning">Best Practices for Log Analytics & Alerts</h2>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Use Meaningful Alert Rules:</strong> Avoid unnecessary alerts by setting precise thresholds.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Regularly Review Log Queries:</strong> Optimize KQL queries for better performance.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Integrate with Incident Management:</strong> Connect alerts to ITSM tools for automated response.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Monitor Alert Fatigue:</strong> Ensure alerts are actionable and do not overwhelm teams.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Leverage AI Insights:</strong> Use Azure Monitor’s AI capabilities for predictive analytics.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Conclusion -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-secondary">Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            Log Analytics and Azure Monitor Alerts are essential tools for proactive monitoring and issue resolution in Azure environments.
            By setting up effective log queries and alerts, organizations can improve performance, security, and operational efficiency.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>
